> TL;DR: Returning a Promise from an async signIn request in one custom Cypress command and doing something with the result in another command does work. While doing the same logic in one Cypress command does not work !?

### Current behavior
I created a custom `login` (below: `logInAndSaveSessionInOneFunction`) command in which I make a signIn call which returns a promise.

`commands.js`:
```js
Cypress.Commands.add("logInAndSaveSessionInOneFunction", () => {
  AuthLib.signIn(username, password).then((data) => {
    cy.setLocalStorage("accessToken", data.accessToken);
  });
});
```
`AuthLib.signIn()` returns a promise.

Then I want to use this command in an `before` block:
```js
  before(() => {
    cy.logInAndSaveSessionInOneFunction();
    cy.saveLocalStorage();
  });
```

I notice that the promise is not resolved. This fails and gives following error message:
```
cypress_runner.js:172286 Uncaught (in promise) CypressError: Cypress detected that you returned a promise from a command while also invoking one or more cy commands in that promise.

The command that returned the promise was:

  > `cy.get()`

The cy command you invoked inside the promise was:

  > `cy.setLocalStorage()`
```

I found this 'related' issue: https://stackoverflow.com/questions/49980311/cypress-io-how-to-handle-async-code where https://www.npmjs.com/package/cypress-promise is referred. But this library cannot be used in `before` or `beforeEach`
 I also read some blogs about Promises and Cypress but couldn't figure it out. 

### Desired behavior
I noticed I can fix this splitting `logInAndSaveSessionInOneFunction` into 2 different cypress commands:

```js
Cypress.Commands.add("login", () => {
  return AuthLib.signIn(username, password);
});

Cypress.Commands.add("loginAndSaveSession", () => {
  cy.login().then((data) => {
    cy.setLocalStorage("accessToken", data.accessToken);
  });
});
```

Using it in my tests:
```js
  before(() => {
    cy.loginAndSaveSession();
    cy.saveLocalStorage();
  });
```

I have no clue why the two commands-way works while doing the same logic in one command fails. 
Can you help me find out why returning a `Promise` in one command and adding `then` in another command works, while doing the same logic in one command does not work ? 


### Test code to reproduce
I created a demo project which you can use to fully reproduce the problem.  
You can find it here:  [https://github.com/Nxtra/Cypress-Amplify-Auth-Example](https://github.com/Nxtra/Cypress-Amplify-Auth-Example)

In `my.test.js` I indicate the above where one case works and the other doesn't.  
As you will see I use AWS Amplify for Auth (Amplify library and Cognito user pool). 
However that should not influence the solution since the problem stems from returning a `Promise` from a Cypress command. 



### Versions
Cypress: 5.3.0
MacOS Catelina: 10.15.6
Browser: Chrome


# Solution

As I mentioned in the comment below, I came up with the following solution:

I figured out how to do this using `cy.then()`

You can do it in one function:
```
Cypress.Commands.add("loginAndSaveSession", () => {
  cy.then(() => AuthLib.signIn(username, password)).then((data) => {
    cy.setLocalStorage("accessToken", data.accessToken);
  });
});
```

or with two functions:
```
Cypress.Commands.add("login", () => {
  return AuthLib.signIn(username, password);
});

Cypress.Commands.add("loginAndSaveSession", () => {
  cy.login().then((data) => {
    cy.setLocalStorage("accessToken", data.accessToken);
  });
});
```

You can find an example here: [https://github.com/Nxtra/cypress-amplify-auth-test/blob/main/cypress/support/commands.js](https://github.com/Nxtra/cypress-amplify-auth-test/blob/main/cypress/support/commands.js)
And some explanation here: [https://www.theclouddeveloper.io/use-cypress-to-test-aws-amplify-apps-with-authentication](https://www.theclouddeveloper.io/use-cypress-to-test-aws-amplify-apps-with-authentication)

