The `route2` method offers fantastic flexibility for working with REST-based APIs. You can filter on URL paths, query parameters, etc. However, it does not offer any options for filtering on the request *body*. I would like to be able to supply a function that inspects the body of a request, and determines if it matches a route or not.

<!-- A clear description of the feature or enhancement wanted in Cypress -->

GraphQL queries are entirely contained in the body of the request. `route2` will filter based on the URL, but (AFAICT) does not allow any filtering on the content of the request.

Ideally, I'd like to be able to write a function that can inspect the request body and indicate to `route2` whether it matches or not. 

For an asynchronous page with multiple GraphQL queries, its impossible to use `route2` to reliably match requests. If a given page makes two different GraphQL queries in indeterminate order (easy to do if those queries depend on when scripts load or previous network requests), then I can't wait on aliased results reliably or call `route2` in such a way that I can always determine if a given request was made.

