Tests that rely on setting and getting the url to be possible to write for @cypress/react

## Other info
This is a roadblock I've been hitting multiple times recently, and I can't see any way around it. Could you please review my scenarios and suggest how I could test these scenarios using @cypress/react? I know I could just test these e2e, but I think there’s immense value in being able to test components in isolation. 

One quick point before listing 2 scenarios, I’ve personally learnt that the following pattern is good - if a component is getting/setting url state, then that url state should be the single source of truth, rather than say setting an equivalent state in react, and updating url as a side-effect. So this belief is my motivation for creating this ticket.

## Scenario 1 - initialising props
A common pattern I use is to have say React Router, with a `/items/:item` route.

Then an `Item` component;
```js
import * as React from 'react'
import { useParams } from 'react-router-dom'

const Item = () => {
  const { data } = useQuery()
}
```

So this `itemId` is the core prop for the component, and I seemingly have no way to set it. I could have defined my components like
```js
const ItemBase = ({itemId) => {
  …
}
const Item = () => {
  const { itemId } = useParams()
  return <Item itemId={itemId}
}
export { ItemBase, Item } // unit test ItemBase, use Item in rest of app
