### Future work

(This has been documented in https://cypress-io.atlassian.net/browse/UNIFY-295)

When we deprecate the legacy APIs/signatures:

- Add a deprecation warning into the `getLegacyDevServer` function that warns when it is called (not when the returned function is called) **OR**
- Update the test runner to add a deprecation warning into the code that requires the plugins/index.js file

When we remove the legacy APIs/signatures:

- Remove the `getLegacyDevServer` function
- Refactor each dev server from this (roughly):

```js
// Legacy signature
module.exports = getLegacyDevServer(devServer, (config) => {
  // code
})

// New signature
module.exports.devServer = devServer
```

To this:

```js
module.exports = { devServer }
```

(Also note that the CRACO `devServer` function will need to be updated to accept the proper `devServerConfig` object)

- Refactor `index.d.ts` types from this (roughly):

```ts

declare namespace legacyDevServer {
  interface CypressFooDevServerConfig {
    // properties
  }

  export function devServer(/* arguments */): Cypress.ResolvedDevServerConfig
}

declare function legacyDevServer(/* arguments */): void

export = legacyDevServer;
```

To this:

```ts
export interface CypressFooDevServerConfig {
  // properties
}

export function devServer(/* arguments */): Cypress.ResolvedDevServerConfig
```

