### Cool stuff

- `defineResult()` allows for automated type definitions for the response
- mutation arguments and returns are strongly typed
- we can use a spy function "as" the resolver instead of "in" the resolver
- since the `mutationResolver` is passed by reference, we can continue setting up resolvers after the component is mounted
- nothing prevents resolving the same mutation twice in the same test with different results. It will be overriden.

