Now, if we want to dynamically assign values to these in our test, and have the following line:
```
Cypress.env({ someVariable: "hello" });
```
So far, everything works, and our new environment variables will look like this:
```
{
  "env": {
    "user": {
      "username": "",
      "password": "",
      "email": ""
    },
    "someVariable": "hello"
  }
}
```
Now if we want to assign a value to the nested variables, we will have something like this:
```
Cypress.env({ user: { username: "world" } });
```
But this will cause the nested variables to be overwritten, and our result is like this:
```
{
  "env": {
    "user": {
      "username": "world"
    },
    "someVariable": "hello"
  }
}
